From 16196a0f5e3304370a3363255f2883b07fb01dc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:04:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 312/314] gallium/pvr: depth testing, colour reload, cached PDS
 programs

- Depth: the render's depth buffer goes through the ZLS (ISP_ZLSCTL,
  ZLOAD_BASE, background depth, zls_stride, DEPTHBUFFER job flag), loaded
  unless cleared in the render and always stored; depth buffers are
  padded to whole 32x32 ISP tiles. The TA ISP state takes the depth test
  and write from the depth/stencil state, and triangle merging is off only
  where the reference turns it off. A full depth clear with a GPU colour
  clear is the background depth instead of a CPU fill.
- A render without a colour clear reloads the target: a load background
  object (texelFetch of the target at its pixel, the target's texture
  descriptor DMAed by a descriptor program), as the reference's load op.
  Before, its previous contents became black.
- Generated vertex-fetch and descriptor PDS programs are cached by the
  bytes their code depends on; draws patch only the data segment.

gltri GLTRI_ZTEST (near triangle, then a larger one behind it after a
mid-frame flush) matches zink at both sample points.
